@coderabbitai I cannot add an additional ownerref to the controller using `ownerreffrom()` as it gives a `controller:true` value which resulted in this error in `e2e-azure-ovn-upgrade` . 

```bash
event happened 193 times, something is wrong: namespace/openshift-console-operator deployment/console-operator hmsg/7e9628ad2d - reason/ServiceAccountUpdateFailed Failed to update ServiceAccount/console -n openshift-console: ServiceAccount "console" is invalid: metadata.ownerReferences: Invalid value: [{"apiVersion":"config.openshift.io/v1","kind":"ClusterVersion","name":"version","uid":"5764b29f-7749-4012-94ce-d8c3d4e72991","controller":true},{"apiVersion":"operator.openshift.io/v1","kind":"Console","name":"cluster","uid":"44ea12d6-4e25-47cb-916f-5127bf971ea2","controller":true}]: Only one reference can have Controller set to true. Found "true" in references for ClusterVersion/version and Console/cluster (17:36:30Z) result=reject 
event happened 192 times, something is wrong: namespace/openshift-console-operator deployment/console-operator hmsg/9ba732befd - reason/ServiceAccountUpdateFailed Failed to update ServiceAccount/downloads -n openshift-console: ServiceAccount "downloads" is invalid: metadata.ownerReferences: Invalid value: [{"apiVersion":"config.openshift.io/v1","kind":"ClusterVersion","name":"version","uid":"5764b29f-7749-4012-94ce-d8c3d4e72991","controller":true},{"apiVersion":"operator.openshift.io/v1","kind":"Console","name":"cluster","uid":"44ea12d6-4e25-47cb-916f-5127bf971ea2","controller":true}]: Only one reference can have Controller set to true. Found "true" in references for ClusterVersion/version and Console/cluster (17:36:30Z) result=reject }
```

However, the logic in the service account controller should ensure that even if we used `ownerreffrom()` that there should only be one `controller:true`.
